  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Replace the single full-page README screenshot with five focused simulated dashboard screenshots\n- Update simulated mode to mock OpenCode, Codex CLI, and Hermes together so README screenshots demonstrate the live multi-source dashboard shape\n- Use live-like model label shapes in simulated screenshots, such as `opencode/...`, `openai/...`, `nous/...`, and `openai-codex/...`\n- Keep the README Usage History screenshot compact by limiting the docs-only capture to six rows while still showing all three tools\n- Reorganize the top-level README around Data Sources, Setup, Screenshots, and short data rules\n- Move detailed Codex/Hermes adapter contracts to `docs/source-contracts.md`\n- Keep screenshot refresh mechanics out of the top-level README; the `--docs` capture mode remains available in `scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py` for maintainers or later docs\n- Add stable section IDs for Tool Sources and Daily Tokens screenshot targets\n- Update API test coverage for multi-source simulated mode only; README screenshot assertions were removed to avoid brittle docs tests\n\nFixes #25\n\n## Validation\n\n- Checked live local API model labels from `/api/usage-history?limit=12` and `/api/models?days=31`\n- `uv run --with playwright python scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py --url http://localhost:8322/?simulate=1 --out docs/screenshots --docs`\n- Visual inspection of all five generated screenshots\n- `uv run python -m unittest tests.test_app tests.test_readme -v`\n- `uv run python -m py_compile app.py scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py dashboard/simulation.py`\n- `scripts/review.sh`\n\n## Guidance used\n\n- GitHub Docs: relative links and image paths are supported in rendered README files\n- W3C WAI: alt text should be concise; longer image explanations belong in surrounding text",
  "changed_files": 14,
